    {
      "id": "lw9hbve",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "A. Agents of Erosion"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Erosion involves both the active breakdown and physical transportation of rock materials by mobile agents.",
        "Primary agents of erosion include running water, wind, glaciers, waves, and groundwater.",
        "River erosion operates through distinct processes such as hydraulic action, abrasion, attrition, and solution.",
        "Material transportation by running water occurs via traction, saltation, suspension, and solution.",
        "Base level defines the theoretical lower limit for land surface erosion by running water."
      ],
      "id": "tu1kq4b"
    },
